# Vercel CLI (drjanduffy.com)

- Install: `pnpm i -g vercel@latest`. Check with `vercel --version`.
- Local replica: `vercel dev --port 3000` (or `pnpm vercel:dev`).
- Deploy-bound / production-like builds: `vercel build` or `vercel build --prod`. Do not use a bare `pnpm build` as the production-build path.
- Keep `package.json` `"build": "next build"`. Vercel runs that script; `"build": "vercel build"` recurses.
- CI auth: set `VERCEL_TOKEN` (and `VERCEL_ORG_ID` / `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID`). Never pass `--token` on the CLI — it leaks in process lists and logs.
- Non-interactive: `--yes`. Confirm live production deploys before running `vercel deploy --prod`.
- Protected previews: `vercel curl`, not disabling Deployment Protection.
- Refresh agent guidance: `vercel agent init --yes` (updates only the marked section in `AGENTS.md`).
